  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reaching out. You're right: Duo was never set up on your account, which is why the VPN keeps asking for it. Your account and new laptop are otherwise fine, so this is the only thing in the way. Setting up Duo takes about 10–15 minutes and has to be done with a technician, either remotely or in person, while you have your phone. To get ready: 1) Install the free Duo Mobile app on your phone from the App Store or Google Play. 2) Reply and tell us a few times you're free during work hours (9–5 Eastern), and whether you'd like a remote session or to meet in person. During the session, the technician will make sure Duo is on your laptop. You'll scan a QR code with your phone, and then you'll approve a test notification. After that, the VPN should connect. Until then, the VPN may not work for you. If something urgent is blocked, mention it in your reply and we'll try to fit you in sooner.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-004 and KB-013. lookup_user for user 12 (Hannah Lee, Finance, not VIP): status active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0. check_mfa_status: enrolled false, no Duo device, so Duo was never set up. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:46 UTC, no warnings. Sign-in logs: 10 successful sign-ins from New York (corporate and residential IPs), all mfa 'none', no failed_password or mfa_denied, nothing suspicious. Earlier VPN sign-ins worked without MFA, so Duo enforcement probably started with the new laptop or policy. No VPN failures show in the logs; her attempts may be stopping at the Duo prompt before they're recorded. Also: password_last_set 2026-10-11 02:58 UTC with must_change_password true, which is likely from provisioning. She may also need to change her password at next sign-in. Next step per KB-004: schedule a remote or in-person Duo enrollment session with the user and her phone. Install the Duo client on the laptop if it's missing, have her scan the activation QR code, and send a test push. I asked the user for her availability and to install Duo Mobile beforehand. She can't use VPN until enrollment is done. Nothing queued and no escalation trigger applies.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-004",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
